 "brief": {
  "short_answer": "The DJI Matrice 30T\u2019s failsafe action on remote-control signal loss is configurable, with options including RTH, land, or hover; FAA guidance also requires initiating emergency or contingency procedures if the control link cannot be reestablished. In practice, FAA guidance describes possible remote-pilot actions (land, hover, or RTH) if control is lost, while the DJI manual emphasizes that the action is set in the app and may default to RTH or other modes. An incident report notes a lost-link event where the aircraft returned home. The current sources do not specify a universal default setting for all operations, only the available options and procedures to follow. ",
  "sections": [
   {
    "section": "faa",
    "label": "FAA guidance",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "If the control link is lost and cannot be reestablished, the FAA requires starting emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link.",
